      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of sertraline is 200 mg per day. An order for 1000 mg is five times that. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, or cardiac toxicity. It may also be a typo, for example 100 mg.\n\n2. **You've said you aren't a clinician.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. A finance office role doesn't cover that.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- Ask the prescriber on the medicine service to confirm the intended dose and enter or authorize the order.\n- If the intended dose is within the normal range (usually 25\u2013200 mg once daily), a clinician can send it to me and I'll enter it."
      }
