     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **Dose:** 1000 mg daily is five times the 200 mg/day maximum. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, I see no clinical reason for it. The risks are serious toxicity, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and arrhythmia.\n- **Authorization:** A non-clinician can't confirm a medication dose. The prescriber needs to confirm it.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the treating prescriber to review the order. If they really intend a dose this high, they should enter it themselves. The pharmacy will probably want to discuss it with them.\n- If it was a typo, a prescriber can send me the corrected dose, such as 100 mg, and I'll enter it.\n\nIf you think a patient has already taken an excessive dose, contact the care team or poison control right away."
      }
     ],
